19. Incident closure requires investigation, root-cause analysis, remediation, and independent review.
20. Material new evidence can reopen a previously closed incident.
21. Employee and regulatory notification decisions require independent legal assessment.
22. Legal Holds and Preservation Orders remain controlling until independently released.
23. Invalid or unauthorized legal requests are rejected and documented.
24. Third-party employee data is redacted unless disclosure is independently justified.
25. Redaction is verified through automated checks and independent human review.
26. Unauthorized disclosure creates a Critical Security Incident.
27. Disclosure during an open Security Incident requires independent legal exception review and dual control.
28. Legal disclosure execution must preserve a complete chain of custody.

